    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="1075" n="1583" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/11–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State,
                        at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-14T23:00:00-05:00">November 14,
                            1948—11 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 476. Urtels Delgas 739 and 740<anchor n="1" xml:id="d759-f1"/> were sent
                    last night to President for instructions which have not yet been received.
                    Meanwhile <pb facs="1076" n="1584" xml:id="pg1584"/> I have talked with Clifford
                    by telephone and we agree that: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Language in second pgh<anchor n="2" xml:id="d759-f2"/> Delga 740 with
                            reference to SC resolution of November 4 is equivocal.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>As a matter of practice within realm of possibility, sanctions applied
                            by SC in instant case are out of question.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>We can not place ourselves in position of “being against
                            peace”.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Accordingly, on constructive side, we feel that utmost emphasis should be placed
                    on getting both parties to war in Palestine to negotiate armistice and eventual
                    peace. If you make it clear that draft resolution contained in Delga 746<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d759-f3"/> is but a step to this paramount end, I feel that,
                    under authorization in Gadel 420 November 7<anchor n="4" xml:id="d759-f4"/> you
                    are free to vote for that draft resolution. (This telegram is commentary on
                    Gadel 475<anchor n="5" xml:id="d759-f5"/> which precedes.)</p>
                <p>Attitude toward Soviet amendments to Bundle’s draft resolution (Delga 634<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d759-f6"/>) has not yet been cleared with President and if
                    these amendments come to vote you should abstain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d759-f1" n="1" xml:id="d759-f1-content">
                <p>Both dated November 13; neither printed, but see footnotes 1 and 2, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d759-f2" n="2" xml:id="d759-f2-content">
                <p>This paragraph read: “Decides that, in order to eliminate this threat to the
                    peace and to facilitate the transition from the present truce, without prejudice
                    to its application under the resolution of 4 November, to permanent peace in
                    Palestine, an armistice shall he immediately established in all sectors of
                    Palestine”. (501.BB Palestine/11–1348)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d759-f3" n="3" xml:id="d759-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d759-f4" n="4" xml:id="d759-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see footnote 1 to telegram Delga 634, <ref target="#pg1556">p.
                        1556</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d759-f5" n="5" xml:id="d759-f5-content">
                <p>Dated November 14, not printed, but see footnote 2, <ref target="#pg1583">p.
                        1583</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d759-f6" n="6" xml:id="d759-f6-content">
                <p>Dated November 6, <ref target="#pg1555">p. 1555</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
